<title> Dynamical Systems and Ergodic Theory (Ph.D. 2025-2026) </title>
<br>
<hr>
<p>
<h2>
PROGRAM (Tentative)<br>
</h2>
<li> Review of the theory of differential equations: global existence and uniqueness of solutions for C^1 and bounded vector fields. 
Floquet theory. Poincar&egrave√sections. Theorem on smooth dependence on initial data and parameters.
<li> Study of the qualitative behavior of solutions of a differential equation on the plane.
<li> Flow box theorem. Stability and Lyapunov functions. Grobman--Hartman theorem. 
Stable and unstable manifolds: Hadamard--Perron theorem.
<li> Concept of genericity for families of vector fields depending on parameters. Generic bifurcations: saddle--node, Hopf.
<li> $\omega$-limit sets and Poincar&egrave--Bendixson theorem.
<li> Differential equations on the (two-dimensional) torus and reduction to the study of circle diffeomorphisms. Rotation number. KAM theorem.
<li> Measurable dynamical systems (definitions and basic examples). Krylov--Bogoliubov theorem. 
Elements of ergodic theory (theorems of Birkhoff, Von Neumann, Poincar&egrave, ergodicity, mixing, ...).
<li> Quantitative statistical properties of dynamical systems: expanding maps and Anosov systems.
<ol>
<br>
Nel caso ci fosse interesse per un diverso argomento relato ai sistemi dinamici, basta chiedere, 
sar&ograve ben lieto di fare cambiamenti al programma.
